1
00:07:54,000 --> 00:08:00,000
TÁR is a music, drama film directed by Todd Field.

2
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:54,000
As celebrated conductor Lydia Tár starts rehearsals for a career-defining symphony,
the consequences of her past choices begin to echo in the present.

3
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Lydia Tár, played by Cate Blanchett.

4
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:42,000
Sharon Goodnow, played by Nina Hoss.

5
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:36,000
Francesca Lentini, played by Noémie Merlant.

6
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:30,000
Olga Metkina, played by Sophie Kauer.

7
00:55:18,000 --> 00:55:24,000
Andris Davis, played by Julian Glover.

8
01:03:12,000 --> 01:03:18,000
Eliot Kaplan, played by Mark Strong.

9
01:11:06,000 --> 01:11:12,000
Tár is a 2022 psychological drama film written and directed by Todd Field.

10
01:19:00,000 --> 01:19:06,000
Cate Blanchett stars as Lydia Tár, a world-renowned conductor, whose
life unravels after she is accused of misconduct.

11
01:26:54,000 --> 01:27:00,000
The supporting cast includes Nina Hoss, Noémie Merlant, Sophie
Kauer, Julian Glover, Allan Corduner, and Mark Strong.

12
01:34:48,000 --> 01:34:54,000
Tár premiered at the 79th Venice International Film Festival in September
2022, where Blanchett won the Volpi Cup for Best Actress.

13
01:42:42,000 --> 01:42:48,000
Following a three-week limited theatrical release, it received a wide
release on October 28, 2022, through Focus Features.

14
01:50:36,000 --> 01:50:42,000
Tár received critical acclaim, especially for Blanchett's
performance and Field's screenplay and direction.

15
01:58:30,000 --> 01:58:36,000
At the 95th Academy Awards, Tár was nominated for
6 awards, including Best Picture.

16
02:06:24,000 --> 02:06:30,000
Blanchett won the BAFTA, Golden Globe, and Critics' Choice Movie Award for Best Actress, and was
nominated for the Academy Award and Screen Actors Guild Award in the same category.

17
02:14:18,000 --> 02:14:24,000
Since its release, it has been regarded as one of the
greatest films of the 2020s and the 21st century.

18
02:22:12,000 --> 02:22:18,000
The film explores themes of infidelity, new york city,
berlin, germany, composer, musician.

19
02:30:06,000 --> 02:30:12,000
The tone is emotional and intense.
